  "fix": {
    "fix_type": "restructure",
    "target_module": "simple_spi",
    "added_latency_cycles": 0,
    "modified_rtl": "  always @(posedge clk_i)\n    if(spe & (|clkcnt & |state))\n      clkcnt <= {clkcnt[11:6] - {5'b0, ~(|clkcnt[5:0])}, clkcnt[5:0] - 6'h1};\n    else\n      case (espr) // synopsys full_case parallel_case\n        4'b0000: clkcnt <= 12'h0;   // 2   -- original M68HC11 coding\n        4'b0001: clkcnt <= 12'h1;   // 4   -- original M68HC11 coding\n        4'b0010: clkcnt <= 12'h3;   // 16  -- original M68HC11 coding\n        4'b0011: clkcnt <= 12'hf;   // 32  -- original M68HC11 coding\n        4'b0100: clkcnt <= 12'h1f;  // 8\n        4'b0101: clkcnt <= 12'h7;   // 64\n        4'b0110: clkcnt <= 12'h3f;  // 128\n        4'b0111: clkcnt <= 12'h7f;  // 256\n        4'b1000: clkcnt <= 12'hff;  // 512\n        4'b1001: clkcnt <= 12'h1ff; // 1024\n        4'b1010: clkcnt <= 12'h3ff; // 2048\n        4'b1011: clkcnt <= 12'h7ff; // 4096\n        default : clkcnt <= 12'hfff;\n      endcase",
    "rationale": "The violating path is clkcnt -> 12-bit ripple-borrow decrementer (clkcnt - 1) -> espr load mux / enable -> clkcnt, all synthesized from lines 240-258 (the 17 unattributed cells are the borrow chain plus the difference XOR and load/enable OAI22). RESTRUCTURE chosen: the serial borrow ripple is broken into two cascaded 6-bit subtracts with a look-ahead borrow. Since the subtrahend is constant 1, the borrow into bit 6 is exactly ~(|clkcnt[5:0]) (a 6-input NOR, depth-3 tree), which drives clkcnt[11:6] - borrow; the low half is clkcnt[5:0] - 1. Concatenation of the two 6-bit results is provably bit-identical to the 12-bit unsigned clkcnt - 12'd1 for all inputs, including the clkcnt==0 wrap to 12'hfff (low=6'h3f, borrow=1, high=6'h3f). Worst-case depth falls from ~15-gate ripple to NOR6-tree + 6-bit ripple, well over the 0.03 ns needed. Latency unchanged, so no reconvergent path (espr mux, |clkcnt/|state enable) needs rebalancing. RETIME rejected: clkcnt is a self-feedback counter; no register exists inside the combinational chain and moving clkcnt around its own loop cannot shorten it. PIPELINE rejected: inserting a stage in a feedback loop would make the counter decrement every two cycles, changing the SPI clock divider ratio, and the reconvergent load/enable logic writing the same flop would also need delaying. NO_FIX rejected: the critical logic is in the shown RTL and has an exact shallower form."
